      <h1>10 Types of Fleece Hoodie Manufacturers in China: How to Pick the Right Factory Profile</h1>
      <p class="ar-meta">
        <span>By <strong rel="author">YAUUM Sourcing Team</strong></span>
        <span>Published <time datetime="2026-10-06">October 6, 2026</time></span>
      <span class="ar-views" data-views-for="/fleece-hoodie-manufacturer-types-china/" data-views-hit></span>
      </p>
      <p class="ar-lede">Fleece hoodies are one of the most forgiving garments to sell and one of the easiest to get wrong at the factory. The fabric hides minor fit problems, the silhouette moves across three seasons, and the margin looks healthy on a spreadsheet. Then a 350 GSM order lands at 290 GSM, or the anti-pilling finish breaks down after three home washes. This guide covers ten manufacturer profiles worth shortlisting, plus the framework for judging whether any of them fits your program.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" data-od-id="article-body">
    <div class="shell ar-grid">
      <article class="ar-body">
        <figure class="ar-figure">
          <div class="sw-ph" role="img" aria-label="Assorted fleece hoodies in multiple colors produced by a China manufacturer">
            <div class="sw-ph-media"><span class="sw-ph-tag">Required image</span></div>
            <div class="sw-ph-copy"><strong>Fleece hoodie lineup</strong><small>Needed: a verified photo of finished fleece hoodies in multiple colors from the production environment.</small></div>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <p>We are YAUUM, a B2B menswear manufacturer producing hoodies, tees, jackets, pants, sportswear, and streetwear. We compete in the same arena as the factories described below, so read this as a working map rather than a neutral ranking. The criteria are the ones we apply to our own line.</p>

        <h2 id="why-china">Why China Still Leads Fleece Hoodie Manufacturing (and What's Changing)</h2>

        <p>China's advantage in fleece is cluster density, not cheap labor. A single hoodie passes through a knit fabric mill, a dyehouse, a fleece-brushing line, a cutting floor, a sewing line, a screen-printing shop, and a packaging supplier. In Zhejiang, Guangdong, and Jiangsu, those facilities often sit within a two-hour drive of each other. That proximity cuts sampling cycles and makes mid-production corrections realistic instead of theoretical.</p>

        <p>Three shifts matter right now:</p>

        <ul class="ar-list"><li><strong>Small-batch, fast-replenishment orders are standard.</strong> Brands that once placed single 10,000-piece orders now split them into 1,000 to 3,000-piece runs to test colorways before committing capital.</li><li><strong>Compliance scrutiny has tightened.</strong> Audit reports and chemical test documentation are requested as a default, not an exception.</li><li><strong>Basic volume has moved to Vietnam, Bangladesh, and Turkey.</strong> That shift is real for plain, high-volume fleece. For complex construction, multi-color graphics, and heavyweight fleece with special washes, China's supplier base remains the deepest.</li></ul>

        <p>If your program involves oversized drop-shoulder fits, puff print, or garment-dyed fleece, China is still the shortest path from concept to shelf.</p>

        <h2 id="criteria">How We Evaluated These Fleece Hoodie Manufacturers (Our Selection Criteria)</h2>

        <p>No public list can tell you which factory will deliver your order. What a list can do is give you a consistent set of questions. We scored every profile below against five dimensions.</p>

        <figure class="ar-figure">
          <div class="sw-ph" role="img" aria-label="Infographic showing criteria for evaluating fleece hoodie manufacturers">
            <div class="sw-ph-media"><span class="sw-ph-tag">Required image</span></div>
            <div class="sw-ph-copy"><strong>Evaluation criteria infographic</strong><small>Needed: a verified infographic built from the five evaluation dimensions listed in this section.</small></div>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <div class="ar-table-wrap"><table class="ar-table"><thead><tr><th>Evaluation Dimension</th><th>Why It Matters</th><th>How to Verify Independently</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Fleece fabric capability</strong></td><td>Determines whether 280–400 GSM brushed fleece, anti-pilling finish, and sherpa are in-house or outsourced</td><td>Request fabric test reports (GSM, shrinkage, pilling grade) and a physical swatch set</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Customization depth</strong></td><td>OEM vs. ODM, print methods, embroidery types, wash finishes</td><td>Ask for a sample of each technique you plan to use, not a catalog photo</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Compliance and audit</strong></td><td>Affects your ability to sell into EU/US retail and marketplaces</td><td>Request the audit report directly and confirm the certificate number with the issuing body</td></tr><tr><td><strong>MOQ and lead time</strong></td><td>Drives cash flow and your ability to test the market</td><td>Ask for MOQ per colorway and per style, plus a written production calendar</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Communication response</strong></td><td>The best single predictor of how a problem gets handled mid-production</td><td>Send a technical question before ordering and measure reply time and specificity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

        <p>The "how to verify" column is not optional: any factory can claim anti-pilling fleece, and the claim is worth nothing without a Martindale or ICI pilling grade on paper. If you need <a href="/hoodie-manufacturer/">custom fleece hoodie manufacturing</a> with a specific print and wash combination, approve each technique on a physical sample before the price conversation starts. Treat the scoring sheet as a filter rather than a verdict, since a factory that scores poorly on compliance can still suit a domestic-only, price-driven program.</p>

        <h2 id="profiles">10 Fleece Hoodie Factory Profiles in China</h2>

        <p>This list is organized by <strong>fit to buyer type</strong>, not by absolute ranking. A factory built for a 500-piece streetwear drop is the wrong choice for a 30,000-piece retail replenishment, and the reverse is equally true.</p>

        <figure class="ar-figure">
          <div class="sw-ph" role="img" aria-label="Fleece hoodie production line in a China garment factory">
            <div class="sw-ph-media"><span class="sw-ph-tag">Required image</span></div>
            <div class="sw-ph-copy"><strong>Production line reference</strong><small>Needed: a verified fleece hoodie production floor photo from the supplied production environment.</small></div>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <h3>1. YAUUM: Full-Category Menswear Manufacturer with In-House Hoodie Development</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> Hoodies sit alongside tees, jackets, pants, sportswear, and streetwear as one of six core categories. A brand building a coordinated drop sources the hoodie, the matching jogger, and the graphic tee on one production calendar instead of chasing three sampling queues. Development covers pullover, half-zip, and full-zip constructions, from regular fits through oversized drop-shoulder blocks.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> This profile fits you if you are launching a multi-category drop rather than a single SKU, or if you want one point of contact across tops and bottoms.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Confirm the exact fleece structure you need (brushed fleece, French terry, or loopback), the GSM band the line runs most consistently, and which print and wash techniques stay in-house.</p>

        <h3>2. Shenzhen-Area Streetwear Specialists: Graphic-Heavy Hoodie Programs</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> A cluster of factories around Shenzhen and Dongguan built their business on graphic-driven streetwear. Their edge is embellishment depth: screen print, DTG, DTF, puff print, flock, and multi-head embroidery under one roof.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> Choose this profile when the artwork is the product and the hoodie sells on the strength of a print or embroidery design.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Request a wash-test sample using your actual print method. Puff print and DTF behave very differently after five home launderings, and the failure mode is invisible in a fresh sample.</p>

        <h3>3. Zhejiang Knitwear Manufacturers: Volume Fleece and Basic Hoodies</h3>

        <p>Zhejiang's knitwear belt is engineered for volume: these plants brush fleece at scale, hold dye lots consistent across large orders, and organize around repeat replenishment rather than one-off drops. If you are an established brand, a retail private label, or a wholesale program with predictable demand, this is the correct profile for 20,000 identical hoodies in three colors. The real risk at volume is lot-to-lot color drift, so ask how they match repeat orders, whether they retain a physical reference standard, and what Delta-E tolerance they work to.</p>

        <h3>4. Jiangsu Full-Package Manufacturers: OEM and ODM Hoodie Development</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> Jiangsu factories generally sit higher on the development curve, offering ODM pattern libraries alongside straight OEM production. If you have a design direction but no tech pack, an ODM-capable partner compresses the path from mood board to fit sample.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> Consider this route if you have no in-house pattern maker and want design input rather than pure cut-and-sew.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Settle ownership of patterns and any design work developed for you. ODM agreements should state in writing what you keep if you move production elsewhere.</p>

        <h3>5. Guangdong Premium Fleece Mills: Heavyweight and Specialty Fleece</h3>

        <p>For 400 GSM and heavier fleece, sherpa linings, and finishes like garment dye and acid wash, a smaller group of integrated mills in Guangdong leads on fabric quality. These are the suppliers behind premium-positioned hoodies that justify a higher retail price on hand-feel alone, which makes them the right match when the fabric itself is the selling point. Because heavyweight fleece shrinks differently from standard weight, get shrinkage data on the exact fabric and finish you are buying rather than a generic spec sheet, and check it after three wash cycles rather than one.</p>

        <h3>6. Fujian Sportswear Manufacturers: Performance and Athleisure Fleece</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> Fujian's sportswear cluster brings technical capability that fashion factories rarely match: moisture management, four-way stretch fleece blends, bonded constructions, and flatlock seaming.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> This profile suits you if your hoodie competes on stretch recovery and moisture management rather than on graphics.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Performance claims need test data. Ask for moisture-wicking and stretch-recovery results on your specific fabric lot, not on a similar fabric from a previous order.</p>

        <h3>7. Shandong Export-Oriented Factories: Cost-Efficient Basic Fleece</h3>

        <p>Shandong plants compete on cost efficiency for straightforward fleece: solid colors, standard fits, minimal embellishment. They are production shops rather than design partners, which makes them a good match for price-sensitive programs, promotional and corporate wear, and any buyer who arrives with a complete tech pack. Before bulk starts, weigh the fabric against your spec, because a quote that undercuts the market by 15% often assumes a lighter fleece than the one you asked for.</p>

        <h3>8. Small-Batch and Fast-Replenishment Studios: Low MOQ Hoodie Production</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> A newer category of smaller workshops built around low-MOQ, fast-turnaround runs. They serve the DTC economy, where a brand needs 100 to 500 pieces to prove a design before scaling. Turnaround is their product; cost per unit is not.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> Start here if you are launching a first hoodie or testing colorways before you can forecast demand.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Low MOQ means higher unit cost and thin negotiating room. Confirm the per-color minimum, the sampling fee, and whether that fee is credited against bulk.</p>

        <h3>9. Integrated Print-and-Sew Factories: All-in-One Hoodie Production</h3>

        <p>Factories combining fabric sourcing, cut-and-sew, and embellishment in one building remove handoff risk, which is why they appeal to buyers who want a single accountable supplier and will pay a modest premium for it. The caution is that "integrated" is a loose claim. Map which steps are genuinely in-house, which are subcontracted, and who owns quality control at each handoff point before you treat the supplier as one vendor.</p>

        <h3>10. Specialist Wash-House Partners: Garment-Dyed and Vintage Fleece</h3>

        <p><strong>Core Strengths</strong> Garment dye, pigment dye, acid wash, and mineral wash create the faded vintage look that commands premium pricing. Far fewer factories run it consistently than claim to.</p>

        <p><strong>Best For</strong> Look here when the wash itself is the design, as it usually is for vintage-inspired labels and premium streetwear.</p>

        <p><strong>What to Verify</strong> Wash results vary batch to batch by nature. Approve a pre-production wash sample and agree the acceptable variation range in writing before bulk dyeing starts.</p>

        <p><strong>Mid-list check-in:</strong> If you are already comparing hoodie programs and want a concrete starting point, <a href="/contact-us/">request a quote and samples</a> from YAUUM. We quote against tech packs for pullover, half-zip, and full-zip fleece in the 280–400 GSM range, and we will tell you plainly whether your spec fits our line.</p>

        <h2 id="which-type">Which Type of Fleece Hoodie Manufacturer Fits Your Business?</h2>

        <p>The list only becomes useful once you map it against your own situation.</p>

        <div class="ar-table-wrap"><table class="ar-table"><thead><tr><th>Buyer Type</th><th>Primary Focus</th><th>Factory Profile That Fits</th><th>Suggested Next Step</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>New brand / first drop</strong></td><td>Low MOQ, sampling support, low financial risk</td><td>Small-batch studios, ODM-capable factories</td><td>Order 2–3 samples across suppliers before committing</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Scaling DTC brand</strong></td><td>Consistent quality, repeatable color, moderate MOQ</td><td>Zhejiang volume knitters, integrated print-and-sew</td><td>Lock a reference standard and a replenishment calendar</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Established retail brand</strong></td><td>Compliance, capacity, delivery reliability</td><td>Zhejiang and Jiangsu volume manufacturers</td><td>Request audit reports and a capacity confirmation</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Premium / fashion label</strong></td><td>Fabric quality, wash depth, construction detail</td><td>Guangdong premium fleece, specialist wash houses</td><td>Approve fabric and wash on physical samples</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Performance / athleisure</strong></td><td>Technical fabric, test data</td><td>Fujian sportswear manufacturers</td><td>Request performance test results</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

        <p>For brands in the first two rows, <a href="/solutions/">small MOQ fleece hoodie production</a> is the right entry point. You pay more per piece and buy the ability to validate a design before locking capital into inventory. Once a colorway proves itself, move it to a volume line and keep the test program running separately.</p>

        <p>One judgment worth stating bluntly: a new brand with no tech pack should not start with a volume factory. The MOQ forces an order size you cannot sell through, and the sampling process assumes you already know exactly what you want.</p>

        <h2 id="mistakes">Common Mistakes When Sourcing Fleece Hoodies from China</h2>

        <p>These are the errors we see most often, usually after they have already cost the buyer money. Browse <a href="/hoodie-manufacturer/#hoodie-styles">our fleece hoodie collection</a> if you want reference specs while reading this section.</p>

        <p><strong>1. Skipping the pilling and shrinkage test.</strong> Anti-pilling is the most over-claimed property in fleece. A hoodie that pills after three washes generates returns and one-star reviews you cannot walk back. Require a pilling grade and a shrinkage percentage measured on your actual production fabric, and keep the report on file.</p>

        <p><strong>2. Treating compliance as a paperwork formality.</strong> Selling into the EU, the US, or major marketplaces makes audit and chemical documentation a gate rather than a nice-to-have. Request <a href="/our-services/">apparel factory compliance &amp; audit</a> documentation before the order rather than after the shipment is booked.</p>

        <p><strong>3. Underestimating sampling time and cost.</strong> Sampling is where the real engineering happens. Buyers who compress it to save two weeks routinely lose two months to production corrections. Budget at least two sample rounds for any new construction, and three if the fit block is new.</p>

        <p><strong>4. Mismatching MOQ to actual demand.</strong> A 3,000-piece MOQ is a bargain per unit and a cash-flow disaster if you sell 800. Confirm MOQ per colorway rather than per style, then model the sell-through against your realistic monthly volume before you commit to the price break.</p>

        <h2 id="how-to-start">Step-by-Step: How to Start a Fleece Hoodie Order with a Chinese Factory</h2>

        <figure class="ar-figure">
          <div class="sw-ph" role="img" aria-label="Step-by-step process of ordering custom fleece hoodies from China">
            <div class="sw-ph-media"><span class="sw-ph-tag">Required image</span></div>
            <div class="sw-ph-copy"><strong>Six-step ordering flow</strong><small>Needed: a verified six-step process diagram for starting a fleece hoodie order, matching the steps in this section.</small></div>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <p><strong>Step 1: Define the spec before you contact anyone.</strong> Write down style (pullover, half-zip, full-zip), fit (regular, relaxed, oversized, drop shoulder), fabric structure and GSM, colorways with Pantone references, embellishment method, labeling, and packaging. A clear spec is the difference between comparable quotes and noise.</p>

        <p><strong>Step 2: Send the RFQ to 3–5 factories and compare like for like.</strong> Ask every supplier the same five questions: MOQ per colorway, unit price at your target quantity, sampling fee and timeline, production lead time, payment terms. Industry-typical ranges for custom fleece hoodies land around 300–500 pieces MOQ per colorway, 7–15 days for sampling, and 30–45 days for bulk, plus 25–35 days of sea freight. Production and shipping run on separate clocks, so build the full calendar end to end.</p>

        <p><strong>Step 3: Develop and approve the sample.</strong> This is where <a href="/production/">fleece hoodie sample development</a> earns its keep. Judge the fabric hand-feel, the fit on a real body rather than a mannequin, the print or embroidery placement, and the wash result. Sign off in writing with dated photos.</p>

        <p><strong>Step 4: Confirm specifications, compliance, and terms.</strong> Lock the tech pack, name the approved sample as the golden reference, collect the compliance documentation, agree the payment schedule, and set the inspection protocol. Nothing should enter production on a verbal agreement.</p>

        <p><strong>Step 5: Produce with in-line quality checks.</strong> Ask for progress photos at cutting, mid-sewing, and finishing. A GSM check on the cut fabric and a seam check at 20% completion catch problems while they are still cheap.</p>

        <p><strong>Step 6: Inspect, ship, and document.</strong> Run a final inspection against the approved sample, confirm packaging and labeling, collect the shipping documents. Keep the golden sample sealed and labeled; the next order depends on it.</p>

        <p>To run all six steps with one supplier across hoodies and coordinating categories, <a href="/contact-us/">start your order with YAUUM</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="faq">Fleece Hoodie Manufacturing FAQ</h2>

        <div class="ar-faq">
          <details class="ar-faq-item" open><summary><h3>What is the MOQ for custom fleece hoodies from China?</h3></summary><p>Most Chinese fleece hoodie manufacturers set MOQ between 300 and 500 pieces per colorway for custom orders, with lower minimums available from small-batch studios at a higher unit cost. MOQ is usually quoted per color, not per style, so a three-color hoodie may carry a three-color minimum. Always confirm whether the sampling fee is credited against the bulk order.</p></details>
          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>How long does fleece hoodie manufacturing and shipping take?</h3></summary><p>Typical timelines run 7 to 15 days for sampling, 30 to 45 days for bulk production after sample approval, and 25 to 35 days for sea freight to major ports. Air freight cuts shipping to roughly 5 to 10 days at a much higher cost. Peak season and fabric availability stretch these windows, so get your dates written into the order confirmation.</p></details>
          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>What GSM fleece is best for hoodies?</h3></summary><p>Most fleece hoodies fall between 280 and 400 GSM. Lightweight fleece around 280 to 320 GSM suits spring and layering pieces; 350 to 400 GSM delivers the heavyweight hand-feel associated with premium streetwear. Above 400 GSM, shrinkage control and sewing difficulty both increase, so confirm the factory has run production at that weight before.</p></details>
          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>What certifications should a fleece hoodie manufacturer have?</h3></summary><p>The relevant certifications depend on your market. Common frameworks cover social compliance audits, quality management systems, and chemical safety standards for textile products. Rather than accepting a list of logos, request the specific report and confirm the certificate number with the issuing body. Match the certifications to the destination market where you actually sell.</p></details>
          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>How much does it cost to manufacture a fleece hoodie in China?</h3></summary><p>FOB pricing spans a wide range driven by fabric weight, embellishment, and order quantity. A 280 GSM solid-color basic sits at the low end; a 400 GSM garment-dyed hoodie with four-color print, custom trims, and special packaging sits at the top, often at several times the price of the basic. Because fabric, print method, and volume all move the number, ask for a quotation against your actual tech pack.</p></details>
          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>How do I verify a factory before placing an order?</h3></summary><p>Request the audit report and confirm its certificate number independently, ask for references or past production examples in your category, order a sample, and test communication responsiveness with a technical question before you commit. A factory that answers slowly or vaguely during the inquiry stage will behave the same way when a production problem appears.</p></details>
        </div>

